  "usedTryThisNowFrames": [
    "ch01 try-this action: Name one trait you inherited from a real person, then write the next visible act that would honor it today.",
    "ch02 try-this action: Before your next interaction, name the likely difficult behavior once, then name the cooperative act you will still perform.",
    "ch03 try-this action: Look at one delayed duty and ask what faculty may weaken if you keep postponing it, then do the first clean step.",
    "ch04 try-this action: Take one obstruction in front of you and write the useful action it now makes possible, not the action it ruined.",
    "ch05 try-this action: When comfort argues for delay, answer with the first duty your role was made to perform, then stand up and do it.",
    "ch06 try-this action: Before choosing the convenient response, ask whether it would still look right if the whole group had to live by it.",
    "ch07 try-this action: When an old irritation returns, state the principle it usually makes you forget, then act from that sentence once.",
    "ch08 try-this action: Pick one complaint you have repeated twice and correct the smallest cause you can touch before explaining it again.",
    "ch09 try-this action: Before correcting someone, write the truthful action needed and the anger you must not add to it.",
    "ch10 try-this action: Choose one name of character you claim, then identify the condition that most often makes you drop it.",
    "ch11 try-this action: When anger rises, run one of the nine checks: what do I know, how have I erred, and what correction serves the whole?",
    "ch12 try-this action: Strip one present problem into matter, form, purpose, and the time within which it will end, then do the just act."
